Keep the voice engine up without its audio device

adm_helpers::Init ended the process (RTC_CHECK, in release builds too) when the audio
device module did not initialize: on Linux, when no sound server answered or one did not
answer in time, the first connection of a call took the whole application down. The
voice engine now logs it and goes on without a device: it plays and records nothing, as
with any other failure of the device, and everything else of the call works.

diff --git a/media/engine/adm_helpers.cc b/media/engine/adm_helpers.cc
index 12dfbc9..7a5f536 100644
--- a/media/engine/adm_helpers.cc
+++ b/media/engine/adm_helpers.cc
@@ -36,7 +36,13 @@ namespace adm_helpers {
 void Init(AudioDeviceModule* adm) {
   RTC_DCHECK(adm);
 
-  RTC_CHECK_EQ(0, adm->Init()) << "Failed to initialize the ADM.";
+  // Fogata: without its audio device (on Linux, no sound server answering, or one
+  // that does not answer in time) the voice engine stays up, and plays and records
+  // nothing: ending the process for it took the whole application down.
+  if (adm->Init() != 0) {
+    RTC_LOG(LS_ERROR) << "Failed to initialize the ADM.";
+    return;
+  }
 
   // Playout device.
   {
